<title>CHILE: Chilgener buys Peruvian power company.</title>
<headline>Chilgener buys Peruvian power company.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean power generator Chilgener has bought into the Peruvian electricity industry with the purchase of 49 percent of Inversiones Dominion Peru SA, owned by U.S. company Dominion Energy Inc, Chilgener said.</p>
<p>Through its Peruvian unit, Dominion owns 60 percent of Peru's Egenor SA, which it bought from the Peruvian government in a privatization process, Chilgener said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;This acquisition signals the beginnning of Chilgener's operations in Peru,&quot; said the statement.</p>
<p>The price was $123 million, said the Chilean company.</p>
